1
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:25,873
Floor Plan 2027 is a home design program that runs in your web browser.

2
00:00:25,873 --> 00:00:29,937
There is nothing to install: you open the page and start drawing.

3
00:00:29,937 --> 00:00:36,733
What you see here is a finished plan of a two-storey family house, seen from above, like an architect's drawing.

4
00:00:36,733 --> 00:00:44,475
Every wall, door, window, piece of furniture and garden object is a separate item that you can select, move and change.

5
00:00:44,475 --> 00:00:49,802
With one click on the 3D view button, the same plan becomes a three-dimensional model.

6
00:00:49,802 --> 00:00:55,492
Here we see the whole house: both floors, the roof, the garden, and even the car in the drive.

7
00:00:55,492 --> 00:00:59,959
You can turn the model with the mouse, to look at it from any side.

8
00:00:59,959 --> 00:01:10,522
Every object has real measurements in metres, so the 2D plan and the 3D model always match exactly.

9
00:01:10,522 --> 00:01:14,145
As you work, the plan is saved automatically in your browser.

10
00:01:14,145 --> 00:01:18,715
You can also save it to a file, or export a picture to print or share.

11
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,198
Let's take a tour of the screen, one area at a time.

12
00:01:22,198 --> 00:01:24,330
This is a new, empty plan.

13
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:26,520
At the very top is the top bar.

14
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:30,441
On the left is the name of your plan: click it to rename the plan.

15
00:01:30,441 --> 00:01:33,549
In the middle are the floor tabs, one for each storey.

16
00:01:33,549 --> 00:01:37,325
On the right are three buttons: Wizard, Demo and File.

17
00:01:37,325 --> 00:01:40,070
Down the left side is the icon library.

18
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:49,665
It holds a hundred and fifty-one icons, sorted into categories: walls and structure, roofs, windows, doors, stairs, furniture, garden and more.

19
00:01:49,665 --> 00:01:53,802
The list at the top shows one category at a time, or all of them.

20
00:01:53,802 --> 00:01:55,800
Below it is the search box.

21
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:00,741
Type a word, such as door or sofa, and only the matching icons are shown.

22
00:02:00,741 --> 00:02:04,832
Tip: right-click any icon to see a small 3D preview of it.

23
00:02:04,832 --> 00:02:06,987
Above the drawing is the toolbar.

24
00:02:06,987 --> 00:02:12,705
On the left are undo and redo, then the zoom buttons and Fit view, which shows the whole plan.

25
00:02:12,705 --> 00:02:19,383
Next come the Show options: Grid, Other floors and Dimensions; and the Assist options: Snap and Align.

26
00:02:19,383 --> 00:02:27,143
Further right are Tidy up, Fill floor and Fill garden, the rotate, duplicate and delete buttons, and the 3D view button.

27
00:02:27,143 --> 00:02:31,299
The large area in the middle is the drawing area, laid out on a grid.

28
00:02:31,299 --> 00:02:36,975
Scroll the mouse wheel to zoom in and out, and drag an empty spot to move the view around.

29
00:02:36,975 --> 00:02:39,287
On the right is the Properties panel.

30
00:02:39,287 --> 00:02:46,604
When something is selected, it shows that object's settings: position, size, rotation, colours and materials.

31
00:02:46,604 --> 00:02:50,731
When nothing is selected, it shows the settings for the whole plan.

32
00:02:50,731 --> 00:02:54,705
The narrow strip between the library and the drawing is the Height bar.

33
00:02:54,705 --> 00:03:00,694
It shows the floor you are working on, and the height above the ground at which new objects are placed.

34
00:03:00,694 --> 00:03:03,108
Along the bottom is the status bar.

35
00:03:03,108 --> 00:03:08,816
It shows where the pointer is, in metres, what is selected, and short tips for using the mouse.

36
00:03:08,816 --> 00:03:17,780
Now that you know your way around, there are three ways to start: watch a demo, let the Wizard design a house for you, or draw your own plan from scratch.

37
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,457
Let's try each one.

38
00:03:19,767 --> 00:03:23,119
The quickest way to learn is to watch a house being built.

39
00:03:23,119 --> 00:03:25,514
Click the Demo button in the top bar.

40
00:03:25,514 --> 00:03:32,886
A window opens with three sample houses: a two-storey family house, a garden cottage, and an L-shaped house.

41
00:03:32,886 --> 00:03:38,986
Each card shows a picture of the finished house, its size, and how many construction steps it has.

42
00:03:38,986 --> 00:03:41,336
Let's pick the Garden cottage.

43
00:03:41,336 --> 00:03:42,752
The demo starts.

44
00:03:42,752 --> 00:03:48,073
Your own plan is put safely aside, and a panel appears at the bottom of the screen.

45
00:03:48,073 --> 00:03:51,123
The panel tells you which step you are on and explains it.

46
00:03:51,123 --> 00:03:57,994
Step one sets out the outline and builds the outer walls, twenty centimetres thick and closed at every corner.

47
00:03:57,994 --> 00:04:04,467
The objects that were just added stay selected, outlined in blue, so you can see exactly what was built.

48
00:04:04,467 --> 00:04:06,467
Click Next to build the next step.

49
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:12,220
Step two lays the floor slab: the concrete base that fills the inside of the outer walls.

50
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,770
Next again.

51
00:04:13,770 --> 00:04:19,869
Step three adds the inner walls, which divide the cottage into rooms.

52
00:04:19,869 --> 00:04:21,858
And step four puts in the doors.

53
00:04:21,858 --> 00:04:27,523
Notice the numbered dots: they show every step, and you can click any dot to jump straight to it.

54
00:04:27,523 --> 00:04:30,056
The Previous button goes back one step.

55
00:04:30,056 --> 00:04:36,055
Instead of clicking Next each time, click Play, and the demo builds the remaining steps by itself.

56
00:04:36,055 --> 00:04:42,680
Watch as the windows, floors, roof, furniture and garden appear, in the order a real house would be built.

57
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,300
The cottage is finished.

58
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,237
Now you have two choices.

59
00:05:02,237 --> 00:05:06,951
Keep this house makes the cottage your own plan, so you can change anything in it.

60
00:05:06,951 --> 00:05:11,259
Exit demo closes the demo, and brings back the plan you had before.

61
00:05:11,259 --> 00:05:14,180
We'll exit.

62
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,242
Next, the House Building Wizard.

63
00:05:16,242 --> 00:05:18,243
Click Wizard in the top bar.

64
00:05:18,243 --> 00:05:24,394
The Wizard asks you a few simple questions, then designs and builds a complete house from your answers.

65
00:05:24,394 --> 00:05:32,531
The questions are listed down the left, and the picture on the right updates as you answer, showing a front view and the layout of each floor.

66
00:05:32,531 --> 00:05:34,681
First, give the house a name.

67
00:05:34,681 --> 00:05:36,507
Then choose what surrounds it.

68
00:05:36,507 --> 00:05:39,704
We'll pick Lawn with trees.

69
00:05:39,704 --> 00:05:46,167
The next question is the size: how wide and how deep the house is on the ground, measured on the outside.

70
00:05:46,167 --> 00:05:50,547
Drag the sliders, or pick one of the quick sizes.

71
00:05:50,547 --> 00:05:57,442
Then the storeys: one, two or three floors, and how high each storey is, from floor to floor.

72
00:05:57,442 --> 00:05:58,742
Now the rooms.

73
00:05:58,742 --> 00:06:01,324
Choose the number of bedrooms and bathrooms.

74
00:06:01,324 --> 00:06:03,299
Let's ask for four bedrooms.

75
00:06:03,299 --> 00:06:09,490
Watch the floor layouts on the right change to make room for the extra bedroom.

76
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:21,886
The next questions let you choose the wall material and colour, the roof style and its covering, the floor finish for each kind of room, and extras such as furniture, a balcony, trees and a parking place.

77
00:06:21,886 --> 00:06:24,396
The last page sums up all your answers.

78
00:06:24,396 --> 00:06:26,929
To change one, click it to jump back.

79
00:06:26,929 --> 00:06:30,830
When you're happy, click Build the house.

80
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:34,749
The house is built on the plan step by step, just like the demo.

81
00:06:34,749 --> 00:06:36,598
Let's press Play and watch.

82
00:06:36,598 --> 00:06:39,229
First the outer walls and the ground slab.

83
00:06:39,229 --> 00:06:42,073
Then the inner walls, the doors and the windows.

84
00:06:42,073 --> 00:06:47,777
Then the upper floor with its stairwell, the stairs, the roof, and finally the furniture and garden.

85
00:07:04,777 --> 00:07:09,635
Change answers takes you back into the Wizard to adjust anything and build again.

86
00:07:09,635 --> 00:07:14,280
We're happy with this one, so click Keep this house.

87
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,214
The house is now your own plan.

88
00:07:16,214 --> 00:07:21,170
Every wall and every piece of furniture can be moved, resized or deleted.

89
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:23,486
Now let's draw a plan ourselves.

90
00:07:23,486 --> 00:07:25,095
Open the File menu,

91
00:07:25,095 --> 00:07:26,605
and choose New plan.

92
00:07:26,605 --> 00:07:37,500
This window sets up the floors before you start: which floors the house has, how high each one is above the ground, the clear height of the rooms, and the thickness of the floor slabs.

93
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:42,478
The defaults are fine for us, so click Create plan.

94
00:07:42,478 --> 00:07:47,497
To add anything to the plan, you drag its icon from the library onto the drawing.

95
00:07:47,497 --> 00:07:54,753
We'll start with the Room icon, which gives you four walls in one go.

96
00:07:54,753 --> 00:07:56,619
The room is now selected.

97
00:07:56,619 --> 00:08:02,428
You can tell by the blue handles around it, and Properties on the right now shows the room's settings.

98
00:08:02,428 --> 00:08:05,441
To set an exact size, type it in Properties.

99
00:08:05,441 --> 00:08:08,860
Click the length box, and type five, for five metres.

100
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,834
Then the width: four metres.

101
00:08:10,834 --> 00:08:16,926
You can also resize the room by dragging its blue handles, or move it by dragging the room itself.

102
00:08:16,926 --> 00:08:18,198
Next, a door.

103
00:08:18,198 --> 00:08:20,487
Click the search box and type door.

104
00:08:20,487 --> 00:08:25,692
The library now shows only doors: plain, double, sliding, folding and more.

105
00:08:25,692 --> 00:08:28,865
Drag the first door onto the bottom wall of the room.

106
00:08:28,865 --> 00:08:36,790
Because Align is switched on, the door fits itself into the wall automatically, and its curved line shows which way it opens.

107
00:08:36,790 --> 00:08:38,649
Windows work the same way.

108
00:08:38,649 --> 00:08:41,861
Search for window, and drag one onto the top wall.

109
00:08:41,861 --> 00:08:43,845
It snaps into the wall too.

110
00:08:43,845 --> 00:08:45,373
Now some furniture.

111
00:08:45,373 --> 00:08:48,632
Search for bed, and drag a double bed into the room.

112
00:08:48,632 --> 00:08:52,782
Then search for sofa, and drag in a sofa as well.

113
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,240
To move an object, simply drag it.

114
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,421
Snap keeps it lined up with the grid.

115
00:08:57,421 --> 00:09:01,399
With the sofa still selected, press R to turn it ninety degrees.

116
00:09:01,399 --> 00:09:03,542
Control D makes a copy of it.

117
00:09:03,542 --> 00:09:06,277
The Delete key removes the copy again.

118
00:09:06,277 --> 00:09:09,118
And Control Z undoes your last action.

119
00:09:09,118 --> 00:09:13,058
You can press it again and again to step back through your changes.

120
00:09:13,058 --> 00:09:15,875
Let's undo the delete, the copy and the turn.

121
00:09:15,875 --> 00:09:17,431
Finally, a floor.

122
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:21,493
Click Fill floor in the toolbar, then click anywhere inside the room.

123
00:09:21,493 --> 00:09:24,815
The floor fills the room exactly, right up to the walls.

124
00:09:24,815 --> 00:09:30,569
In Properties you choose its material: wood planks, parquet, tiles, carpet, stone and more.

125
00:09:30,569 --> 00:09:34,668
Let's pick parquet.

126
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,769
Ready to see the room in 3D?

127
00:09:36,769 --> 00:09:38,629
Click the 3D view button.

128
00:09:38,629 --> 00:09:43,761
The 3D view opens in place of the plan, with its own toolbar along the top.

129
00:09:43,761 --> 00:09:47,761
Drag with the mouse to turn around the room,

130
00:09:47,761 --> 00:09:50,475
and scroll the mouse wheel to zoom in or out.

131
00:09:50,475 --> 00:09:55,175
Click Cut walls to lower the walls, so you can look into the room from outside.

132
00:09:55,175 --> 00:09:58,741
Now the furniture and the parquet floor are easy to see.

133
00:09:58,741 --> 00:10:01,672
Top looks straight down from above, like the plan.

134
00:10:01,672 --> 00:10:07,003
Eye level puts you inside the room, two metres above the floor, as if you were standing there.

135
00:10:07,003 --> 00:10:09,603
Perspective takes you back to the normal view.

136
00:10:09,603 --> 00:10:13,277
Any change you make on the plan is shown in 3D as well.

137
00:10:13,277 --> 00:10:19,452
To go back to the plan, click Close 3D, or press Escape.

138
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:23,187
Give your plan a name: click the name at the top left, and type.

139
00:10:23,187 --> 00:10:25,247
You don't have to remember to save.

140
00:10:25,247 --> 00:10:33,457
The plan is stored in your browser automatically as you work, so if you close the tab, it is still there the next time you open the page.

141
00:10:33,457 --> 00:10:36,399
To keep a copy of your own, use the File menu.

142
00:10:36,399 --> 00:10:41,029
Save, or Control S, downloads the plan as a dot JSON file.

143
00:10:41,029 --> 00:10:43,948
Keep it as a backup, or send it to someone else.

144
00:10:43,948 --> 00:10:46,525
Open loads a saved file back in.

145
00:10:46,525 --> 00:10:53,687
Export SVG and Export PNG save a picture of the drawing, which you can print or email.

